WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Summary of previous episodes</b>

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.370
<i>Last time on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>:</i>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.900
<i>Snow-niisan is sick.</i>

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.440
<i>The landlord went to the 
mainland to find some medicine,</i>

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.790
<i>but we were all so desperate to do something,</i>

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.790
<i>we went out to find out if there 
was medicine on the island.</i>

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.090
<i>Apparently Suishi-neesan stayed at home,</i>

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.250
<i>and went looking for 
medicine on the Internet.</i>

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.680
<i>But she couldn't use her mind-reading 
powers on people she couldn't see.</i>

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.430
<i>In a suspicious chatroom 
full of anonymous people,</i>

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.430
<i>someone who claimed to have
 the medicine reached out to her,</i>

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.030
<i>so Suishi-neesan went alone to meet them.</i>

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.270
<i>It was a dangerous thing to do,</i>

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.230
<i>but the person who knew about the medicine</i>

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.890
<i>turned out to be 
Sumire-chan's class teacher,</i>

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.240
<i>who runs a secondhand shop 
and knows our landlord.</i>

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:58.200
<i>Suishi-neesan can be surprisingly reckless.</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
<b>Frankenstein Family</b>

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.490
<b>#10: Split</b>

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.180
I'm sure Snow-niisan will be happy

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.110
knowing what you did for him...

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.360
We're back!

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.190
Where's Snow-niisan?

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.820
He's gotta be asleep upstairs, right?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.850
He's not here.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.310
This is bad!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.790
The moon sure looks pretty tonight!

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.380
What?

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.870
Am I drunk?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.720
Day one, one thousand steps... day two...

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.480
Whoops!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.390
Have you seen a lost boy?

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.320
No.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.330
Let's try this way.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.290
Have you seen this man?

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.650
No.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.730
<i>She's cute.</i>

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.090
Let's get some pasta.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.160
A monster!

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.900
Heaven help me!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.230
What's the matter?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.400
Get away from me!

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:13.160
I'm scared! Get it away!

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.030
Dammit...

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.580
I won't give up!

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:11.000
<i>It's my turn to search for </i>you<i>, Snow-niisan!</i>

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.870
Stop that! It tickles!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.200
Hey, stop that!

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.380
Stop!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.680
Stop it! Tanisu will be mad!

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.680
Stop it!

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:58.850
Are you okay?

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.310
Does something hurt?

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:17.480
Wait!

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.400
Huh?

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.340
Are you all right?!

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.740
Thank you...

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.330
Are you hurt?!

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:10.980
Um...

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.410
Aren't you... that boy's big brother?

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.860
Mister!

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.380
Are you okay?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.230
Thank you. I'm fine now.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.520
I'm glad to hear it. I'm fine, too.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.790
But where did that wolfman go?

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.290
You should probably rest...

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.570
You're right.

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:20.570
Sumire-chan is nice to everyone. 
Because she's an angel.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.410
It's not happening.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.240
No sense in averting your 
eyes from the truth.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.750
Sumire loves Snow.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:35.050
You're wrong.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.200
She will some day, then.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:40.150
Liar.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:46.090
If you don't have the courage 
to face facts, what can you do?

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:50.180
Use that big brain of yours.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:53.070
It's an easy problem to solve, isn't it?

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:58.150
Monsters can't live with humans, right?

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.860
Your life so far has proved it, hasn't it?

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:05.660
All your hard work has 
basically been pointless.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:11.410
The only reason your landlord is nice to you

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.830
is because he doesn't 
know what you really are.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:19.480
You know that better than anyone, don't you?

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:22.460
What you want is impossible.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:26.030
That's why you're hiding what you are, right?

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.680
You're wrong. I'm sure that someday, 
my brother and sisters will...

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:40.870
"Someday, they will." You might 
as well say they <i>never</i> will.

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.310
When is the "someday" you speak of?

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:48.360
Tomorrow? Next week?

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.360
Next month? Next year?

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.690
In ten years?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:13:01.930
What really matters is that Sumire 
would never accept a monster family.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:08.470
They all just do what they want, 
anyway. They don't care about you.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.930
You should live with that 
kind of honesty, too.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.040
Choose.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:20.120
Your ideal life, or that 
monster family of yours?

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.610
<i>That was some kind of mistake.</i>

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:24.390
<i>But...</i>

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:27.860
<i>Don't avert your eyes from the truth.</i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:32.680
<i>If you don't have the courage 
to face facts, what can you do?</i>

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:35.500
Shut up!

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:54.120
<i>No... I need to make the medicine 
that will make them human.</i>

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:55.310
<i>And then...</i>

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.830
It's your fault, y'know?!

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.830
So, what if it is?

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.170
What answer has Tanisu reached?

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:25.960
<b>Frankenstein Extras!</b>

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.680
<i>Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.240
<i>Today's theme is...</i>

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.960
<b>Today's theme is...</b>

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.880
Let's go to the flipboard!

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:28.670
Okay!

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.010
Ta-da!

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.590
"How's the teamwork among the main cast?"

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.650
Teamwork?

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:55.560
<b>How's the teamwork 
among the main cast?</b>

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.800
I think we have good teamwork!

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.430
I think it's amazing.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.270
"It's amazing!" She says.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:46.910
The teamwork is surprising. On the mic, 
this is very real during recording.

00:16:46.910 --> 00:16:48.140
We have to swap the mic a lot.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:49.860
Yeah, that's true.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.400
This way and that.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.580
Our Senpais move it.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.120
They're nice.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.520
I think Hayami-san and I are totally in sync.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:59.210
Yeah, I agree.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:01.240
Everyone thinks that.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:04.370
That was a little exciting.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.800
I want us to be the same.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:22.190
<i>To talk together.</i>

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:23.890
<i>To eat together.</i>

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.890
<i>To play together.</i>

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.810
<i>To sleep together.</i>

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.190
<i>Because...</i>

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:34.610
<i>since the day we were born...</i>

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.070
<i>we have always been together.</i>

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:39.610
<i>Even if our powers are different,</i>

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:42.920
<i>we know.</i>

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.550
<i>We are the same!</i>

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.540
Everyone's teamwork really is great.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.090
Even if you're pushed out a little,

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.560
you still chime in from the back.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.200
That's true.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:57.340
We compromise in our conversations.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:01.760
Whenever we're eating, Hayami-san
 always says, "We are family, after all!"

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.970
It makes me so happy!

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.850
I love her like a mother.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:09.050
Yeah, I love her.

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:10.620
I think we have a lot of teamwork.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.940
That's all we can say, really.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.190
Yeah, that's all we can say...

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:20.710
But when we returned to 
the institute we came from,

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:23.200
we all use our powers in our own ways.

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:25.770
I think I was very useful, myself.

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:26.540
You used it.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.220
Looking for people and such.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:33.080
I go all around, jumping up
 to high places and such.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.000
That's right. We all did that together.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.590
It's open here.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.070
Okay...

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.140
The camera's not working.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.070
Okay!

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.520
You want me to go?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:24.920
Suishi also. She reads minds.

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.640
She helps Tanisu.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:31.250
They help each other, don't they?

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:35.860
Sui-chan. Could you take us
 to Tani-chan right now?

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:41.360
Beneath this cliff.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.450
Tanisu is there.

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:50.410
To find him, we'll need someone 
with extreme physical capabilities.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:52.990
Aisuri-neesan is the only 
one who could do it.

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:54.490
We need you.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.660
You're all so darn sad.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.120
I'll find him in no time!

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.350
Nicely done.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.940
Tanisu has no sense of direction.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:18.290
That's right.

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:23.150
He has no sense of direction, so 
while he's kind of their caretaker,

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:26.280
he's still a little 11-year-old boy.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:30.890
He tries hard to keep them all together,

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.120
but there are some things 
he can't keep up on,

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.380
and things he can't handle.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:38.640
So his siblings help him fill in the gaps.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:39.520
That's true.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:44.970
When they search for Tanisu, 
they all work together.

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:48.620
Hey, Tanisu!

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:52.310
Aisuri-neesan...

00:20:58.260 --> 00:20:59.400
You idiot.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.780
I'm hungry!

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.860
You trying to starve me to death?!

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.470
I'm sorry...

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:31.810
Let's go.

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:35.390
If we don't hurry, I'll have to eat <i>you</i>.

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:38.600
So much teamwork.

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:39.970
They have teamwork.

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.520
There's teamwork in the story, too.

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.710
Yeah, there is. Seriously.

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:46.130
But when you think about 
that, Tanisu is useless.

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:48.530
That's not true! He's a genius!

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:51.740
The others couldn't get along without Tanisu.

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.510
A genius!

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:54.120
True. He's a genius. Yes.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:56.120
He goes shopping.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:58.650
Yeah, because we have no common sense.

00:21:57.050 --> 00:21:58.650
He goes shopping.

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:01.590
Going shopping... that's ordinary!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.920
Yes, it's normal.

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:05.300
But it's hard to do ordinary things.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:07.050
He's the only one who can do ordinary things.

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:17.020
You shouldn't have gotten so high and mighty.

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:20.100
Don't defy me again, okay?

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:22.010
You're all really amazing.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:24.040
You bet your butt!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:27.990
Thank you, Aisuri-neesan.

00:22:30.170 --> 00:22:31.490
What the heck...

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:39.350
Hey, what are we going to do for dinner?

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:42.050
Don't worry. I'll work it out.

00:22:42.050 --> 00:22:43.270
Cup ramen, huh?

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:45.920
Sounds great! Let's have it!

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:48.320
He can't always follow through.

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.090
He's adorable.

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:53.080
That's why he can't live 
without his siblings.

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:55.000
And that's true the other way around, too.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:57.290
They would really fall apart without Tanisu.

00:22:57.290 --> 00:22:58.440
Hooray!

00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:01.240
In that sense, they support each other.

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:03.290
They do, and we do.

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:05.880
We all have teamwork going.

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:05.880
True!

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:06.700
We went full-circle!

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:07.690
We did!

00:23:07.370 --> 00:23:08.550
Thank goodness.

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:13.450
<i>At last, the story reaches its climax!</i>

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:16.740
<i>Next time on </i>Frankenstein Family<i>:</i>

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:18.480
<i>In preparing for the finale,</i>

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:22.460
<i>let's have a special episode, looking 
back on what we've done as a family!</i>

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:27.210
<b>Kano and Akatsuki Rin appear!</b>

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:27.210
<i>We'll also have a special 
edition of Frankenstein Extras!</i>

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.010
It feels like we're family.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:33.390
I'm not sure if I should be saying this...

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:36.260
Make sure you watch it!

00:23:33.570 --> 00:23:37.680
<b>Next time, a special before the final episode!</b>

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.890
Was that an imitation?
